        <div class="reason__intro">
          <p class="eyebrow">Why BHIC exists</p>
          <h2>Progress should not cost a people their memory.</h2>
          <p>Roads, oil and opportunity are changing Buliisa. We make sure Bugungu knowledge, places and voices help shape what comes next.</p>
        </div>
        <figure class="reason__image"><img src="/assets/1f69baf799a27ca3.webp" alt="BHIC staff and community members exchange knowledge in conversation under a tree" loading="lazy"></figure>
        <div class="work-list" id="work" aria-label="What BHIC does">
          <article><span>01</span><div><h3>Record living memory</h3><p>We work with elders and knowledge holders to document stories, songs, place names, crafts and practices.</p></div></article>
          <article><span>02</span><div><h3>Bring heritage into schools</h3><p>Heritage clubs help young people encounter local knowledge as something living, useful and their own.</p></div></article>
          <article><span>03</span><div><h3>Care for the museum</h3><p>Objects, photographs and oral accounts become starting points for conversation between generations.</p></div></article>
          <article><span>04</span><div><h3>Defend cultural rights</h3><p>Community knowledge helps Bugungu voices take part in decisions about land, culture and the future.</p></div></article>
        </div>
      </section>

